<title>USA: Culbro jumps on spin-off news.</title>
<headline>Culbro jumps on spin-off news.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Investors applauded Culbro Corp's plan to publicly sell shares of its General Cigar Holdings unit, pushing the stock up 2-3/8 to 60 in midday trading.</p>
<p>While Culbro previously said it was mulling ways to raise equity capital, traders said the decision to spin off the General Cigar unit will give the company more focus.</p>
<p>If the cigar unit offering is successful, Culbro said it also may distribute to its shareholders shares of its non-tobacco businesses. The non-tobacco units include its nursery business, most of its New England real estate holdings and other investments.</p>
</text>
